course: dictionary
lesson: 12364
title: Crocodilian: animals of the crocodile family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A crocodilian is any animal in the crocodile family group. Crocodiles, alligators, caimans and gharials are all crocodilians. Use it as a noun, like «The crocodilian slid into the river without a sound.»
explain: The word can also be an adjective, meaning like a crocodile or to do with crocodiles. Look at the clues around it. «Her crocodilian grin made the little boy step back.» A grin is a smile, and a crocodile has a very wide mouth, so a crocodilian grin is a wide, scary smile.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you think crocodilian means a kind of fish, try «The fish slid into the river» and see whether the sentence still makes sense with the animal you know. Context and a quick check help you decide.
fact: A crocodilian is any animal in the crocodile family: crocodiles, alligators, caimans and gharials.
fact: Crocodilians are large reptiles with armoured skin, strong jaws and long tails.
fact: Crocodilians live in rivers and swamps of warm countries.
fact: Crocodilians are close relatives of birds and of dinosaurs.
fact: In Australia, saltwater crocodiles live in the north. Always obey crocodile warning signs and never swim where they live.
exercise: «The crocodilian lay still on the muddy bank, waiting.» What is a crocodilian? | A bird that cannot fly | A plant that grows in swamps | A kind of fish that lives in the sea | *An animal in the crocodile family
exercise: Which animals are crocodilians? | Dolphins and whales | Frogs and toads | *Alligators and caimans | Penguins and owls
exercise: «Her crocodilian grin made the little boy step back.» What does crocodilian suggest here? | A happy song | *A wide, scary smile | A cold wind | A sleepy yawn
test: «Crocodilian skin is armoured, so it is very tough.» Which of these is a crocodilian? | Snake | Tortoise | Frog | *Gharial
test: Where do crocodilians usually live? | Deep in the snow | In the desert sand | On the tops of mountains | *In rivers and swamps of warm countries
exam: Which statement is true? | Crocodilians have no tails | Crocodilians live only in cold lakes | *Crocodilians are close relatives of birds | Crocodilians are a kind of plant
